+## Full-transfer replay plan preparation
+
+`replay.py` prepares the five existing BGE cases for the measured native replay
+entry point. It never submits a device job, queries device occupancy, regenerates
+data, opens the original inline-weight model, or changes CPU golden/expected
+outputs. Run the normal `data` and `build` stages first; it reads their persisted
+NPYs and the exported ONNX IO metadata. `BGE_MODEL_PATH` is unnecessary here.
+
+```bash
+python3 models/bge/replay.py --prepare-only \
+  --config models/bge/config.yaml --device 10 \
+  --output-dir work/bge/replay/baseline-2027 \
+  --instances 1 --seed 2027 \
+  --min-seconds 60 --max-seconds 300 --min-requests 10000
+```
+
+The preparation root must be new. It receives `inputs.bin` and `plan.json`;
+`plan.output_dir` points to its **not yet created** `runtime/` child so a managed
+launcher can require a new results directory. The exported graph defaults to the
+config artifact; `--graph /absolute/path/to/exported/model.onnx` selects an
+already packed, external-weight graph without loading its weights. The CLI
+requires the original INT64/FP32 input contract and FP32 `[1,10112]` scores.
+
+The default is all cores even if the YAML contains a historical core limit.
+Use `--aicore-num '12|24'` for an explicitly selected AIC/AIV pair. Change
+`--instances` and `--precision-mode` explicitly for candidates; these options do
+not modify the YAML or validation thresholds. `--capture` records every measured
+output and its request manifest for an independent correctness run. Capture
+includes disk work between requests and must not be used for official QPS.
+
+`--preload /absolute/path/to/fusion.so` may repeat. It appends libraries to the
+inherited allocator/preload string in `plan.runtime_env.LD_PRELOAD`; it does not
+set the Python process's environment or load those libraries while preparing.
+The managed native launcher must apply `runtime_env` to the **native child only**
+and preserve the inherited allocator. Do not prefix the Python CLI with a
+fusion `LD_PRELOAD`.
+
+After reviewing the plan, submit it through the workflow's existing managed
+`run_checked.py` / `device_job.py` wrapper, which checks the physical device,
+occupancy, lock, timeout and remaining budget. The launcher runs the frozen
+`runtime/build/ge_runtime` with this plan on stdin. This preparation command does
+not establish that the selected device is free, and it has no unmanaged `--run`
+mode. Events, runtime results and optional capture data belong under `runtime/`;
+keep them associated with the plan and native binary identity.
+
+CPU-only preparation regressions:
+
+```bash
+python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_bge_replay_cli.py -v
+```
